<section class="hcm-or-section hcm-or-alt" id="features"><div class="hcm-or-wrap-sm">
<div class="hcm-or-hd"><span class="hcm-or-eyebrow">Feature Fit Guide</span><h2>Bodyfriend Features to Test Before You Buy</h2></div>
<p style="margin-bottom:18px">Bodyfriend chairs can feel very different from model to model, so features should be tested in person when possible. Pay attention to the massage feel, massage intensity, gravity recline, gravity positioning, foot and calf comfort, and whether the chair's <strong style="color:var(--ink)">multi massage auto programs</strong> are easy for you to use.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:18px">If you are comparing advanced models, ask an HCM specialist to explain the difference between XD-Pro and <strong style="color:var(--ink)">XD massage</strong> feel, how the chair handles deep tissue-style pressure, whether the model includes <strong style="color:var(--ink)">leg stretch</strong>, and whether features such as <strong style="color:var(--ink)">safety sensors</strong> or a <strong style="color:var(--ink)">Bluetooth speaker</strong> are available on the exact model you are considering.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:22px">Do not assume every Bodyfriend model has the same feature package. Confirm the product page, showroom unit, warranty details, and current availability before buying.</p>
